17	/*
18	 * tool_emotion_motion.c — IMU fall / upright detection (emotion toy).
19	 *
20	 * Algorithm v5, driven by 8 groups of measured QMI8658 data
21	 * (docs/fall_detection_design.md): tilt angle vs. a FIXED upright
22	 * reference — the dock-posture baseline b = (0, -1, 0) of design doc
23	 * §5.1 — gated by a quasi-static condition.  No boot calibration:
24	 * the v4 boot-time baseline could lock onto a wrong posture (device
25	 * held in hand / already lying flat at boot, doc §8.6), and every
26	 * restart re-learned it.  With the reference fixed, detection starts
27	 * on the very first frame.  Gyro magnitude is deliberately NOT
28	 * a trigger — spinning the toy around the gravity axis reaches 490
29	 * rad/s, above every measured fall impact (277~417 rad/s).
30	 *
31	 * State machine:
32	 *   MONITORING     quasi-static AND theta > 60° vs. the fixed reference
33	 *                  for 500ms -> FALLEN.
34	 *   FALLEN         injects a help prompt via voice_channel_inject_prompt
35	 *                  (PROACTIVE turn; retried while voice is not ready);
36	 *                  quasi-static AND theta < 30° for 3s -> upright event +
37	 *                  thanks prompt -> MONITORING; 30s untouched -> timeout.
38	 *   FALLEN_TIMEOUT silent until one quasi-static theta < 30° frame (the
39	 *                  toy was really picked up) re-arms MONITORING.
40	 *
41	 * Quasi-static: |a| in [0.8, 1.2] g AND |gyro - offset| < 30 rad/s.
42	 * The gyro zero-rate offset is HARD-CODED (doc §3.2: stable across
43	 * posture & temperature; a few rad/s of unit-to-unit error is noise
44	 * against the 30 rad/s gate).  Accel unit is g, NOT m/s^2 — a resting
45	 * device reads ~0.98.
46	 */
